cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Commodity Intelligence: Release-Aware Commodity Nowcasting with True Point-in-Time Data"
message: "If you reference this research, its original figures, or its empirical findings, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Koogjin"
    alias: Koogjin
repository-code: "https://github.com/Koogjin/steel-scrap-forecast-demo"
abstract: >-
  A release-aware nowcasting study of monthly U.S. commodity producer price
  indexes (iron and steel scrap, iron ores, crude petroleum). Forecasts are
  updated at five within-month cutoffs (W0-W4) using only information that was
  actually published by each cutoff, reconstructed from official release
  calendars. The study separates the incremental predictive contribution of
  target history, target-specific market/industry information, and officially
  documented material events, and reports rigorous negative evidence for the
  event layer.
keywords:
  - nowcasting
  - point-in-time data
  - commodity prices
  - producer price index
  - forecast vintages
  - information release timing
  - reproducible research
version: "V11"
date-released: 2026-08-29
